'''PHP2Shell''' ('''CVE-2026-109618''' and '''CVE-2026-109619''') is a [[Vulnerability (computer security)|vulnerability]] reported in October 2026 in the common web scripting language [[PHP]]. While the information about the vulnerability has been embargoed until 21 October at 14:00 UTC,<ref name="Website-3" /> unconfirmed leaks claim that it allows [[arbitrary code execution]] on any website that runs PHP versions 5 through 8.<ref name="Website-1">{{Cite web |last=Goodin |first=Dan |date=2026-10-21 |title=PHP warns it plans to release 2 emergency patches imminently |url=https://arstechnica.com/security/2026/10/php-maintainers-tell-web-devs-to-prepare-themselves-for-critical-security-patches/ |access-date=2026-10-21 |website=Ars Technica |language=en}}</ref>

[[File:Wikimedia Phabricator PHP2Shell.png|thumb|Wikimedia's [[Phabricator]] as seen hours before the patch, having been disabled as a precaution]]

The vulnerability was rated 9.2 (critical) out of 10 under [[Common Vulnerability Scoring System|CVSS]] v4.0 by PHP developers.<ref>{{Cite web |title=php.announce: [ANNOUNCE] Upcoming Critical PHP Security Release |url=https://news-web.php.net/php.announce/509 |access-date=2026-10-21 |website=news-web.php.net}}</ref> Early reporting suggested versions as early as PHP 5, all the way through to PHP 8, are affected,<ref name="Website-2">{{Cite web |title=Rapid Response: php2shell, Leaked Critical PHP Vulnerabilities (CVE-2026-109618 & CVE-2026-109619) |url=https://www.huntress.com/blog/php2shell-leaked-critical-php-vulnerabilities |access-date=2026-10-21 |website=Huntress |language=en}}</ref> with an emergency patch scheduled for release on 21 October at 14:00 UTC together with all other information about the vulnerability.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-10-20 |title=PHP: News Archive - 2026 |url=https://www.php.net/archive/2026.php#2026-10-20-1|access-date=2026-10-21 |website=www.php.net |language=en}}</ref><ref name="Website-2" />

It is notable for the fact that the PHP maintainers announced the update early and before release,<ref>{{Cite web |title=Critical vulnerabilities in PHP {{!}} Stay tuned for php2shell mitigation and patches |url=https://www.aikido.dev/blog/critical-vulnerabilities-in-php-php2shell |access-date=2026-10-21 |website=www.aikido.dev |language=en}}</ref> encouraging users to prepare and update as soon as the patch was released. One security firm, Sansec, expected "mass attacks to start within 15 minutes of the release".<ref name="Website-1" /> PoCs, write-ups, and partial mitigations started circulating on the Internet.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Only for the curious... |url=https://jackalsyn.com/posts/php-up-2026.html |access-date=2026-10-21 |website=jackalsyn.com}}</ref>{{Better source needed|reason=The current source is insufficiently reliable ([[WP:NOTRS]]).|date=October 2026}} [[Cloudflare]] has reported signs of early exploitation prior to public patch release, and deployed temporary [[web application firewall]] (WAF) rules as an attempted stopgap mitigation against the vulnerability.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Knecht |first1=Dane |title=Dane Knecht 🦭 (@dok2001) on X |url=https://x.com/dok2001/status/2112811965735202970 |website=X (formerly Twitter) |date=21 October 2026}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=2026-10-21 |title=Hold on to your butts: Web admins braced for emergency PHP updates to plug leaked exploits |url=https://www.pcgamer.com/software/security/we-expect-mass-attacks-to-start-within-15-minutes-of-the-release-web-admins-braced-for-emergency-php-updates-to-plug-leaked-high-severity-holes/ |access-date=2026-10-21 |work=PC Gamer |language=en}}</ref>

